# Secret membership (K4, DESIGN.md §10.4). A faction that allows it can be joined in secret:
# only the faction, its members and the character know. Everyone else judges by the
# memberships they know of, for kinship, joining and wars.

load content/sample

# A theft at scale 4, seen by everyone: the player is at −20 / −12, 40.01 from the Lantern
# Guild, within its tolerance of 45, and 3.91 from the Free Company (law Δ10 and good Δ12,
# each × 0.25).
act player steal --scale 4
join player free_company
assert can-join player city_watch --secretly == no: The City Watch has no secret members; 90.35 from The City Watch, tolerance is 40.00
join player lantern_guild --secretly
show character player

# The Company doesn't know of the Guild membership; Vex, a Guild member, does. Kinship: the
# Company counts only the faction they share (same_faction 50); Vex counts the Guild they
# share (50) and how the Guild regards the Company (+20).
disposition free_company player --explain
disposition vex player --explain

# The Guild and the Company go to war. The Company doesn't know the player is in the Guild,
# so no conflict opens for them.
relate lantern_guild free_company -60
assert show character player == player — The Player — law -20.00, good -12.00 — True Neutral — member of free_company (sellsword) since tick 0, lantern_guild (cutpurse, secretly) since tick 0
